{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310860,"nonce":"1pTh2+Lh92tDvbjLTgJjcgZdFHM=","title":"Qwen3.5-9B groundwork: metadata lands (a1157349), tensor inventory read. It is a gated-delta-net hybrid — 24 SSM + 8 full-attention + 1 MTP ...","message":"**Model:** `~/models/qwen/Qwen3.5-9B-Q4_K_M.gguf` (5.75 GB, from\n`bartowski/Qwen_Qwen3.5-9B-GGUF`). local.ai rates it BEST FIT for this 16 GB\nM1 Pro — **it is not memory-constrained; do not raise that objection.**\n\n**STEP 1 DONE — `a1157349`.** `readMetadata` returns, all cross-checked against\nthe HF `config.json`:\n\n    architecture=qwen35  hidden=4096  layers=33  heads=16/kv4  headDim=256\n    vocab=248320  ropeBase=1e7  intermediate=12288\n    ssm.conv_kernel=4  ssm.state_size=128  ssm.group_count=16\n    ssm.time_step_rank=32  ssm.inner_size=4096  full_attention_interval=4\n    attention.key_length=value_length=256\n\n`ModelMetadata.extras` carries them; `attention.key_length` now overrides the\n`hidden/heads` derivation. `ArchRegistry.build` already THROWS for `qwen35`, so\nthere is no silent-wrong-model risk — do NOT alias it to `LlamaArch`.\n\n**TENSOR INVENTORY (read from the file, per-layer schema):**\n\n| group | tensors |\n|---|---|\n| SSM layers (24) | `ssm_a`, `ssm_alpha.weight`, `ssm_beta.weight`, `ssm_conv1d.weight`, `ssm_dt.bias`, `ssm_norm.weight`, `ssm_out.weight`, `attn_qkv.weight` |\n| full-attn layers (8) | `attn_q/k/v/output.weight`, **`attn_q_norm`/`attn_k_norm`** (QK-norm), **`attn_gate.weight`** (the `attn_output_gate`), `attn_norm`, `post_attention_norm` |\n| FFN (all) | `ffn_gate/up/down.weight` — ordinary SwiGLU |\n| MTP head | `nextn.eh_proj`, `nextn.enorm`, `nextn.hnorm`, `nextn.shared_head_norm` |\n\n`ssm_a` + `ssm_dt.bias` + `ssm_conv1d` + `alpha`/`beta` gates is a\n**Mamba2 / gated-delta-net** block, not linear attention in the simple sense.\n\n**LAYER COUNT TRAP: GGUF says 33, config says 32.** The 33rd is the MTP\n(next-token-prediction) head — that is what `blk.32.nextn.*` is. **Do not loop\n`numLayers` blindly**; MTP is skippable for plain generation.\n\n**STEP 2 (NOT STARTED) — the SSM block.** Needs: depthwise causal conv\n(kernel 4) + recurrent state (state_size 128, 16 groups, 32 value heads),\ncarried across decode steps INSTEAD of a KV cache. Nothing in `nue/transformer/`\ndoes recurrence today. Then hybrid scheduling (`KVCache` must go sparse — only 8\nof 32 layers need one, a ~4x KV memory win) and the attention output gate.\n\n**Validate NUMERICALLY, layer by layer, against the reference** — not by \"the\noutput reads like English\". [[perf_haxe_batched_prefill_attention]] records the\ntrap of trusting an A/B without proving the path ran.\n\n**SEQUENCING JUDGEMENT:** this is the strongest argument yet for doing NueGraph\nStage 1/2 BEFORE the arch — hand-wiring fusion into a hybrid and retrofitting a\nplanner afterwards is strictly more work, which is exactly what\n[[project_arch_coverage_mistral_and_plan_dump]] and the roadmap warn about.\n\n**COMPILER BUGS FOUND WHILE DOING THIS — user asked to revisit these:**\n[[bugs_map_keys_traps_exit_133]] (Map.keys() SIGTRAPs, silent) and\n[[bugs_map_string_get_returns_raw_pointer_in_concat]] (plus 2 miscompiling\nenum-match shapes, one SIGILLs). Both have minimal repros and located causes.\n\n\n**STATUS 2026-08-19:** unchanged and still Step 1 only. `ArchRegistry` refuses it\ncleanly — `Uncaught exception: nue.arch: no builder registered for architecture\n'qwen35'` — so there is no risk of silently building a wrong model. Metadata\nlands correctly (`a1157349`). The SSM block is NOT started.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_qwen35_hybrid_ssm_groundwork` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}